{"pages":[{"w":612.0,"h":792.0,"s":[[13.889,2.206,18.17,3.8,3.431,"EQUINOX"],[13.889,5.306,14.953,1.205,1.078,"Q U A N T I T A T I V E"],[69.444,2.807,14.011,1.643,1.471,"US Equity Research"],[69.444,4.27,11.266,1.46,1.307,"14 November 2026"],[13.889,10.995,14.159,3.651,3.268,"Duolingo"],[13.889,14.731,40.75,2.373,2.124,"Users are back; the money has yet to follow"],[13.889,20.845,52.964,1.809,1.634,"Duolingo’s bet is paying off in users. In February it gave up over $50m of"],[13.889,22.289,52.957,1.809,1.634,"bookings to cut friction for free learners; daily active users (DAUs) then grew"],[13.889,23.733,52.931,1.809,1.634,"21%, 23% and 29% in Q1-Q3, and Q4 is guided similar to Q3. The shares rose"],[13.889,25.177,52.951,1.809,1.634,"26% the day after Q3 results (3 November) and are 88% above April’s low,"],[13.889,26.621,52.931,1.809,1.634,"though 69% below the May-2025 peak. Money lags users: Q3 bookings rose"],[13.889,28.065,52.931,1.809,1.634,"12%, paid subscribers 14% (28% at end-2025) and Adjusted EBITDA fell 2% to"],[13.889,29.509,41.83,1.809,1.634,"$78.7m. Bookings per DAU fall 13% this year on our estimates."],[13.889,31.995,52.934,1.809,1.634,"1) Q4 bookings are $391m against $382m guided, the Q1-Q3 average beat. 2)"],[13.889,33.439,52.964,1.809,1.634,"Q4-average DAUs grow 20% and 15% in 2027-28E to 94m, short of"],[13.889,34.883,52.934,1.809,1.634,"management’s 100m goal. 3) Paid subscribers grow 14% and 13%; bookings per"],[13.889,36.328,52.934,1.809,1.634,"subscriber stay flat as the top Max tier closes. 4) Adj. EBITDA margin recovers"],[13.889,37.772,52.959,1.809,1.634,"from 26.6% to 27.0% and 28.5%. Bookings then grow 12% and 14%, 2027E"],[13.889,39.216,52.931,1.809,1.634,"revenue is $1,387m (consensus $1,393m) and EPS is $2.75, $3.21 and $4.05 in"],[13.889,40.684,52.934,1.809,1.634,"2026-28E. Stock compensation is 14% of revenue: after it, 2026E EBITDA is"],[13.889,42.128,26.266,1.809,1.634,"$152m, not $326m. Cash is $29 a share."],[13.889,44.59,52.962,1.809,1.634,"Our Dec-27 target of $140 averages two methods, both after stock"],[13.889,46.034,52.931,1.809,1.634,"compensation. A 28x EV/EBITDA, midway between today’s 39x and the 17x"],[13.889,47.502,52.964,1.809,1.634,"median of Netflix, Spotify, Match, Pinterest and Reddit, on 2027E EBITDA of"],[13.889,48.946,52.934,1.809,1.634,"$178m plus cash gives $129. A DCF (10% cost of equity, 3.5% terminal growth)"],[13.889,50.39,52.964,1.809,1.634,"plus cash gives $153. At today’s price a 10% return needs revenue growth of"],[13.889,51.834,52.934,1.809,1.634,"12% a year in 2030-36; we assume 12% fading to 6%. We rate the shares"],[13.889,53.278,52.934,1.809,1.634,"Underweight (Neutral: −5% to +15%). Upside risks: faster conversion, lower"],[13.889,54.722,48.999,1.809,1.634,"app-store fees. Downside: DAU growth fading as one-off campaigns lapse."],[13.889,57.21,13.042,1.643,1.471,"Price Performance"],[15.758,66.579,0.999,1.022,0.915,"50"],[15.268,64.622,1.489,1.022,0.915,"100"],[15.268,62.665,1.489,1.022,0.915,"150"],[15.268,60.708,1.489,1.022,0.915,"200"],[15.268,58.751,1.489,1.022,0.915,"250"],[18.176,67.273,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Jan 26"],[22.815,67.273,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Apr 26"],[27.668,67.273,2.47,1.022,0.915,"Jul 26"],[32.276,67.273,2.96,1.022,0.915,"Oct 26"],[18.423,68.444,4.868,1.275,1.111,"Duolingo ($)"],[26.072,68.444,7.626,1.275,1.111,"S&P 500 (rebased)"],[20.549,69.604,1.972,1.387,1.209,"YTD"],[25.559,69.604,1.433,1.387,1.209,"1m"],[30.017,69.604,1.433,1.387,1.209,"3m"],[34.446,69.604,1.984,1.387,1.209,"12m"],[15.277,70.67,1.691,1.387,1.209,"Abs"],[19.845,70.67,2.597,1.387,1.209,"-5.8%"],[24.089,70.67,2.811,1.387,1.209,"18.0%"],[28.547,70.67,2.811,1.387,1.209,"14.7%"],[33.19,70.67,3.148,1.387,1.209,"-11.4%"],[15.492,71.735,1.476,1.387,1.209,"Rel"],[19.293,71.735,3.148,1.387,1.209,"-16.3%"],[24.089,71.735,2.811,1.387,1.209,"21.1%"],[28.547,71.735,2.811,1.387,1.209,"17.8%"],[33.19,71.735,3.148,1.387,1.209,"-23.6%"],[13.889,73.592,15.839,1.643,1.471,"Valuation (